  "rationale": "The batch exposes a reusable noun-phrase gap: after a determiner, a noun may follow directly or after adjectives. The representative prefix “The” strongly favors other nouns while “apples” has almost no matching mass; similar direct determiner-to-noun contexts target pears, needles, and end, and a determiner-plus-adjective context targets day and village. Add moderate-weight noun rules for this visible suffix pattern rather than encoding particular stories or names. This is not a claim that every determiner must be followed by a noun: other continuations, including adjective continuations, remain valid, and the added mass may be less appropriate in unusual or incomplete prefixes. No new head is needed because the prefix POS sequence expresses the pattern directly.",
